; Anifight -- character and stage selection list.
;
; There are no generated characters. Every entry below is a community
; character that you obtain yourself into local_chars/ (gitignored); the line
; here reserves its cell, and the folder makes it playable. docs/COMMUNITY.md
; is the list and the instructions.
;
; To add a character, drop its folder into local_chars/ and add a line here.
; Nothing else needs to change:
;
;     [Characters]
;     kfm/kfm.def
;
; The format is:
;
;     charname, stage1, stage2, ...
;
; where an entry may also be `randomselect` (a random-character cell), and
; optional parameters may follow, e.g. `music = song.mp3`, `hidden = 1`.
; A second def inside a character's folder is selected with a slash:
;
;     kfm/alt-kfm.def, stages/training.def

[Characters]
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Kung Fu Man, and why he is still here.
;
; He is Elecbyte's own reference character and the only one a stock MUGEN
; install is guaranteed to have. This game measures every other fighter against
; him as well: his standing art is the height the whole roster is normalised to
; (see `kReferenceStandingHeight` in engine/fighter.cpp), so a roster without
; him has nothing to be the size *of*.
kfm/kfm.def

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Dragon Ball.
;
; The roster is Dragon Ball and nothing else, which is a decision about the
; fight rather than about taste: these are edits of edits, published by
; different authors over twenty years, and their art arrives at every scale from
; 70 pixels to 200 for the same declared height. Left alone, the biggest of them
; is half again the size of the smallest and reaches half again as far, and the
; two are not a match. Normalising the art brings them to one size, and keeping
; the roster to one series keeps the *look* consistent too -- a 1998 hand-drawn
; sprite and a 2015 redrawn one sitting in the same match read as a bug even
; when they are the same height.
;
; All thirteen come from Mugen Free For All's Dragon Ball series thread --
; https://mugenfreeforall.com/topic/51078-dragon-ball-series-part-1/ -- which
; indexes them by the author of each edit. Every entry names a folder in
; local_chars/; the author is recorded here because these are edits of edits and
; the thread is the only place that says whose is whose.
;
; The def files were renamed from whatever the archive called them (several
; carried spaces and accented characters) so that folder, line and file all read
; the same. Nothing inside a def depends on its own filename.
;
; Three of these are separate Vegettos rather than one character with three
; forms, because that is how they were published: they have unrelated sprites,
; animations and movesets and no code in common.
dbz_goku/dbz_goku.def              ; SSJ Goku -- SSJTrunks
dbz_gohan/dbz_gohan.def            ; P-Gohan ssj2 -- Barrado
dbz_vegeta/dbz_vegeta.def          ; Vegeta (base) -- HiddenSage121
dbz_gogeta/dbz_gogeta.def          ; Gogeta -- Supermystery
dbz_piccolo/dbz_piccolo.def        ; Piccolo -- Ssonic
dbz_gogeta_ssj4/dbz_gogeta_ssj4.def      ; Xeno Gogeta SSJ4 -- Orochi Shin
dbz_vegeta_ssj4/dbz_vegeta_ssj4.def      ; Vegeta SSJ4 -- Ryon, edited by Kenjiro44
dbz_vegeta_bal/dbz_vegeta_bal.def        ; Balance SSJ4Vegeta -- Linkgamer2004
dbz_vegeta_ssg/dbz_vegeta_ssg.def        ; Vegeta SSG -- Sustina, edited by GOD984
dbz_vegetto/dbz_vegetto.def              ; Vegetto, transforming -- ThiaggoAssis
dbz_vegetto_ssj/dbz_vegetto_ssj.def      ; Super Vegetto SSJ -- Mr. 4x3l
dbz_vegetto_ssb/dbz_vegetto_ssb.def      ; Vegetto -- Adoriendson Tenorio
dbz_yamcha/dbz_yamcha.def                ; Yamcha -- Mr. 4x3l

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; What used to fill the rest of the grid, and why it does not any more.
;
; Twenty-one entries used to sit below these: ronald, peter, homer, naruto,
; mario, sonic, chuck, rareakuma, omegatomhanks, evilryu, evilken, dio, donald,
; hulk, batman, deadpool, scorpion, kratos, godzilla and masterhand, plus a
; second goku. None of their folders is obtainable from a free-to-use source,
; so all twenty-one loaded as empty cells -- a grid two thirds black boxes, and
; a cursor that had to be told to step over them. They reserved cells for
; characters that were never going to arrive.
;
; Five more followed: Giorno, Kira, jolyne_asb, mista and s_diavolo, from
; amarimono's MUGEN work (https://github.com/amarimono-mugen/products). Those
; did load. They were dropped for being the wrong series rather than for being
; wrong -- a roster is a set of fighters that look like they belong in the same
; game, and JoJo stands next to Dragon Ball the way a photograph stands next to
; a drawing.
;
; The grid is still four rows of ten. Room is the point: the thread above is
; "part 1", so more Dragon Ball fighters are expected, and a grid that grows
; into empty cells at the end costs nothing -- the cursor steps over them
; (`moveoveremptyboxes = 0`) and the select screen does not draw a plate for a
; cell with nothing in it.

; Extra stages are available in VS and Watch modes.
; The pool a match falls back to when the chosen fighter names no stage of
; its own. Order matters: the first that loads is the default arena.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The MUGEN install's roster.
;
; These arrived with the MUGEN 1.0 folder in the player's own Downloads: twenty-
; seven characters, each with the .snd file it was written for, so their voices
; and effects are their authors' rather than anything synthesised here. They are
; in local_chars/ (gitignored, like everything third-party) and nothing about
; them was changed to make them load -- they are read the way MUGEN reads them.
;
; Five of them still trip the AI test's freeze check, all for the reason noted
; under Helper in docs/COMMUNITY.md; they load and fight, and their own AI can
; loop when it is pressed point-blank for long enough.
mugen_black/Black.def   ; Goku Black -- Mikel8888 (142 MB)

mugen_evil_goku/Evil Goku.def   ; Goku -- Gohvu (95 MB)

mugen_g6_kakashi_kid/G6_Kakashi_Kid.def   ; Kakashi Kid -- CobraG6 (41 MB)

mugen_g6_naruto_sennin/G6_Naruto_Sennin.def   ; Uzumaki Naruto Sennin -- CobraG6 (53 MB)

mugen_genos/Genos.def   ; Genos -- BlackJudai (36 MB)

mugen_hinata/Hinata.def   ; Hinata -- Monkey_D._Yomi (9 MB)

mugen_izuku_midoriya/Izuku Midoriya.def   ; Izuku Midoriya (Deku) -- Rivelio, Edit TrafalgarLawzz (58 MB)

mugen_levi/Levi.def   ; Levi -- Mikel8888 (42 MB)

mugen_madara_rikudou/Madara_Rikudou.def   ; Uchiha Madara -- Mikel8888 (26 MB)

mugen_meliodas/Meliodas.def   ; Meliodas -- Mikel8888 (29 MB)

mugen_minato/Minato.def   ; Minato -- Midoriya707 (Edited by InSeph) (25 MB)

mugen_naruto/Naruto.def   ; Uzumaki Naruto -- Mikel8888 (62 MB)

mugen_naruto_ashura_jus/Naruto_Ashura_JUS.def   ; Naruto -- Mikel8888 (55 MB)

mugen_naruto_sennin_jus/Naruto_Sennin_JUS.def   ; Naruto -- Mikel8888 (39 MB)

mugen_sai/Sai.def   ; Sai -- Salah (21 MB)

mugen_saitama/Saitama.def   ; Saitama -- Salah (70 MB)

mugen_sasuke_hebi_white/Sasuke_Hebi_White.def   ; Sasuke -- Mikel8888 (27 MB)

mugen_shisui/Shisui.def   ; Uchiha Shisui -- Salah (49 MB)

